# Backlog / Future Work

## Review Follow-Ups

- Optional: make benchmark environment failures explicit instead of silently printing `Unknown`. Address by logging the WMI/CIM exception message or HRESULT in the benchmark header when system info queries fail.

## Test Infrastructure

- **Admin test runs hang on exit (historic; not reproduced in the last two attended runs)**: `run-coverage.ps1` (full mode) or `native-coverage.ps1` launched elevated via UAC has intermittently failed to exit cleanly after `dotnet test` reports all tests passed, with the parent shell sitting indefinitely on `Start-Process -Wait`. This is a different failure mode than the build-start hang (it happens after tests pass, not at build start). Not reproduced in the 2026-07-13 or 2026-08-22 attended runs - two clean runs, not proof the underlying issue is gone. If it recurs, prior investigation narrowed the suspects to:
  - `WatchUsnJournal_*` admin tests use `CancelIoEx` to unblock a kernel wait - possible the cancel races with process teardown and leaves a worker thread in a non-signaled wait, blocking the runtime's exit.
  - The `dotnet test` host process (`testhost.dll`) running under instrumentation may not flush the coverage file before the parent reaps it.
  - Long-term remedy if it recurs: split admin-only tests into a separate test project so the non-admin run stays the default and elevated runs can be opted into with a known-stable test set.

## Packed Index Follow-Ups (deferred)

- **Children table (CSR)**: revisit when measured tree UI expand latency exceeds 50 ms.
- **Name interning**: revisit when the measured name pool exceeds 40 percent of block size.
- **Secondary name index**: revisit when a warm `FindByName` query exceeds 200 ms; sidecars are keyed by block generation.
- **Subtree exclusion**: revisit when a user asks.
- **Hard links as multiple rows per record**: revisit when a consumer needs the second name.

## CI / Build Follow-Ups (deferred)

(Preserved 2026-06-19 from the reaped Gitea-CI plan/spec docs. CI is live; these are known residual items.)

- **Gitea artifact REST API gap**: `actions/upload-artifact@v3` succeeds but Gitea's `/api/v1/.../artifacts` endpoint returns `total_count: 0`. Artifacts upload but are not retrievable via REST. Gitea limitation; acceptable since branch protection gates on job status, not artifacts.
- **Tag-triggered release / benchmark workflow**: not yet designed; revisit when 0.4 ships.
